  ROW ALIGNMENT LOOKS CORRECT. The matrix's abundant genes are the 
  ones skin should express, so GAPDH reading low is a property of 
  this assay rather than a join error. Visium 3' capture on FFPE 
  does vary by gene and probe set, and GAPDH is not a reliable 
  reference here -- which is itself worth knowing, since it means 
  ACTB and B2M should carry the quantification control. 

